{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102388-gambling-in-cofd","id":1102388,"title":"Gambling in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T15:42:12-07:00","id":1102388,"title":"Gambling in CofD","content":"There is a player who's envisioning his character as someone with a gambling problem. Since gambling will undoubtedly come up during play, how would you go about representing it in game, mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T18:01:20-07:00","id":1102402,"title":"","content":"In vampire the requiem there is an addicted persistent condition. You could apply that to the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T18:01:21-07:00","id":1102403,"title":"","content":"You could consider ait a lingering Addicted Condition. Furthermore, gambling issues lead to money issues so alternatively you could create a Gambling Problem Condition:<br /> <br /> Source: your character is addicted to gambling, he gambles at least once a week and loses a lot of money on regular basis<br /> <br /> Resolution: gain one point of Integrity and decide to resolve this condition instead<br /> <br /> Beat: You're broke this week and therefore you're unable to spend any money on some equipment/rent/ whatever leading to a story complication","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T18:03:56-07:00","id":1102404,"title":"","content":"A gambling problem is best represented as a persistent Condition, giving a Beat when the character bets and loses something he shouldn't.<br /> <br /> For actual gambling? Depends on the game. If it's something with an element of skill, like poker, contested rolls for the &quot;big pot&quot; of the night should work. For games like craps or blackjack, I'd drop the d10s and play a literal round of the game, with normal dice or a deck of cards. For betting on sports events, the idea is to predict the result from the past performances of the contestants, which looks like a research task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T18:09:19-07:00","id":1102405,"title":"","content":"There's a sidebar exactly for this in the Winter Masques supplement for Changeling 1ED, page 97.<br /> <br /> It's basically an Extended and Contested Intelligence + Composure + Equipment vs Intelligence + Composure + Equipment roll. Odds favor the house (flat -3 to -5 penalty to gamble gainst it) and whoever is better at reading the situation/cheating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:41:19-07:00","id":1102630,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, for the replies. I'm kind of out and away flrom my books and my computer, so I've been delayed in my reply.<br /> <br /> Well, my initial thought were how to resolve gambling/games mechanically (as in what checks to make). I didn't initially think about the longer term effects of the gambling problem. <br /> <br /> In regards to the Addiction condition - did it make it into the CoD Core Rulebook? I don't remember seeing it. I do remember deprived,which seems like it could also work. Also, I remember looking it up for a NPC. But I don't recall he Addicted condition. It does appear in the GMC pdf, though (and I can access it on my phone).<br /> <br /> Back to mechanics for a second, while I agree that it would be an extended and contested Intelligence + Composure, could it be something else as well? Since many consider poker being a bluffing game, could Intelligence + Subterfuge, for example, be used in that extended and contested action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T17:54:28-07:00","id":1102662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Dynel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1102388-gambling-in-cofd?p=1102630#post1102630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the Addiction condition - did it make it into the CoD Core Rulebook? I don't remember seeing it. I do remember deprived,which seems like it could also work. Also, I remember looking it up for a NPC. But I don't recall he Addicted condition. It does appear in the GMC pdf, though (and I can access it on my phone).</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see it in the Core Book, I mainly remember it from the VtR 2e core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T18:13:04-07:00","id":1102669,"title":"","content":"Addicted is in Demon, Vampire, Mage, Beast, Promethean and the free God-Machine Chronicle update available <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Chronicles of Darkness has Deprived, which is more mechanically disabling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-11-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T21:06:44-07:00","id":1102701,"title":"","content":"If you want to mechanically represent two opponents matching skills at the table I recommend using a series of rolls made by each competitor;<br /> 1-Intelligence + Academics to represent the research and statistical analysis angle.<br /> \u200b2-Wits + Empathy to read your opponents tails.<br /> \u200b3-Manipulation + Subterfuge to hide your own tails and to represent bluffing.<br /> 4-(Optional) Dexterity + Larceny vs Perception to represent actual cheating with the caveat that if you try and fail on this roll the cost will be severe and all other rolls won't matter.<br /> \u200bBoth sides make the rolls and unless one failed at cheating they tally the number of successes rolled, the higher number wins.<br /> This would serve as a short cut way to represent all of the various ways in which players compete without playing out every draw or bluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T02:09:53-07:00","id":1102739,"title":"","content":"If I would run Gambling scene, I would just go with slightly modified <i>Chase Rules</i> from <b>CoD Rulebook, </b>page 84 of it. It let's you use various dicepools from roll to roll, but if you are not using those of now winning side, you are at slight ( but riding ) disadvantage. Then you can easily use any of dicepools from @<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\">2ptTakrill</a> post. Just set Terms of Success, starting probably from 5 minimum. We could help make Terms Table here, in this topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}